## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design EU-resident, privacy-conscious analytics pipelines using serverless components, ensuring tenant isolation and practical cost controls.

## Key Concepts

- API Management as secure, centralized ingress boundary
- Event Hubs for reliable, scalable ingestion
- Functions for idempotent, serverless processing
- Cosmos DB (SQL API) with tenantId partitioning and TTL for retention
- Power BI DirectQuery for near-real-time dashboards
- Azure AD RBAC for per-tenant isolation
- Key Vault-backed BYOK and encryption-at-rest
- Cost controls: autoscale, reserved capacity, budgets

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: pseudocode for a Function that writes to Cosmos DB
const { CosmosClient } = require('@azure/cosmos');
const client = new CosmosClient(process.env.COSMOS_ENDPOINT, process.env.COSMOS_KEY);
async function handleEvent(event) {
  const tenantId = event.tenantId;
  const item = { id: event.id, tenantId, ...event.payload, ts: Date.now() };
  await client.database('TenantDb').container('Events').items.upsert(item);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test idempotency and exactly-once processing?
- How would you enforce per-tenant data residency and prevent cross-tenant access?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical Azure-native data path design, governance, and cost controls for a multi-tenant SaaS.

## Key Concepts
- REST ingestion with serverless compute (Azure Functions)
- ADLS Gen2 with tenant-prefixed folders for per-tenant isolation
- Data Factory for hourly pipeline orchestration
- Purview for data governance and lineage tracking
- Synapse for analytics and Azure ML for anomaly detection
- Paired region DR and budget-based controls for data residency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Azure Function to trigger Data Factory pipeline on schedule
export default async function (context, req) {
    const pipelineRunner = await context.executionContext.getBindingData();

    const response = await fetch('https://management.azure.com/subscriptions/{subscription-id}/resourceGroups/{rg}/providers/Microsoft.DataFactory/factories/{df}/pipelines/WeatherIngestionPipeline/createRun?api-version=2018-06-01', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
            'Authorization': `Bearer ${process.env.ARM_TOKEN}`,
            'Content-Type': 'application/json'
        }
    });

    context.log('Pipeline triggered:', response.status);
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses your ability to architect a scalable, cross-region analytics platform that enforces strict tenant isolation, data governance, and cost discipline while maintaining near real-time processing capabilities.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-region active-active design and disaster recovery strategy
- Per-tenant data isolation using storage prefixes and role-based access control
- Ingestion via Event Hubs; processing with Databricks and Delta Lake
- Data governance with Purview; encryption with customer-managed keys
- Cost optimization through auto-scaling and resource tagging

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Spark job configuration for per-tenant partitioning
spark.conf.set("spark.sql.shuffle.partitions", "200");
spark.conf.set("spark.databricks.delta.optimizeWrite.enabled", "true");

// Read tenant-specific data
df = spark.read.format("delta")
  .load(f"abfss://tenant-{tenant_id}@storage.dfs.core.windows.net/")
  .filter(col("tenant_id") == tenant_id);

// Write with tenant partitioning
df.write.partitionBy("tenant_id")
  .format("delta")
  .mode("append")
  .save(f"abfss://processed@storage.dfs.core.windows.net/analytics");
```
